    {
      "id": "tew2uoo",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Mineral Resources"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Minerals are naturally occurring substances with a definite chemical composition, classified into metallic, non-metallic, and energy resources.",
        "The Chota Nagpur Plateau serves as the richest mineral belt in India, often termed the mineral storehouse of the country.",
        "Major metallic minerals produced in India include iron ore, manganese, bauxite, and copper, forming the backbone of heavy industries.",
        "Energy resources are categorized into conventional sources like coal and petroleum, and non-conventional sources like solar and wind power.",
        "Sustainable management and recycling are imperative for the conservation of non-renewable mineral resources."
      ],
      "id": "rtd5f1s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "97902nw",
      "content": "• Minerals are natural substances found in rocks."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "own3vfc",
      "content": "• They are formed through geological processes over millions of years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ie34haz",
      "content": "• Minerals are essential raw materials for industries."
    },
