    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Chota Nagpur belt is frequently tested regarding its rich deposits of iron ore, coal, mica, and manganese.",
        "Gondwana coal deposits account for nearly 98% of India's total coal reserves and are mainly found in river valleys like Damodar, Mahanadi, and Godavari.",
        "Digboi (Assam), Bombay High (Maharashtra), and Ankleshwar (Gujarat) are major petroleum centers frequently featured in map-pointing and direct questions."
